From: libpldm portable build maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] polyfills: Include the header declaring std::launder

Developed against upstream be4f63e36408921e76d868593176377de84e945e,
after patches 1-5 in this series.

The lifetime polyfill uses std::launder, declared by <new>. Do not rely
on <memory> including it transitively: libc++ configurations without
that incidental include fail when building the base unit tests.

diff --git a/polyfills/start_lifetime_as.hpp b/polyfills/start_lifetime_as.hpp
--- a/polyfills/start_lifetime_as.hpp
+++ b/polyfills/start_lifetime_as.hpp
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 #pragma once
 
 #include <memory>
+#include <new>
 
 /*
  * C++23 [obj.lifetime] `std::start_lifetime_as` is not yet implemented in
